 ### Escape Pods
 
-- All Pods start Locked. They unlock manually (Items, Hatch Control System) or automatically (first Character death; Self-Destruct reaching a yellow space).
-- To enter: use the Evacuation Section A/B Room Action (see Player Reference) — pay the Room Action cost of **2 Action cards**, and the Pod must be **Unlocked with a free Character space** in that Section. A Noise roll is required first, and you cannot enter if any Intruder or a Malfunction token is in the Evacuation Section Room. Each Pod holds up to 2 Characters.
-- After entering, either **launch immediately** or **wait**. Launching (now or on a later turn) removes your miniature and the Pod token from the game — you no longer participate; a launched Pod's occupants are always treated as having arrived on Earth. Entering and waiting passes the current turn. At the start of your first round in the **next Player Phase**, choose: stay and pass; launch; or exit for free into the corresponding Section Room and play a full round of 2 Actions (FAQ Rules 2). Waiting Characters count as present in that Room for Noise rolls from bag development (FAQ Rules 1). A later Malfunction in the Section does not affect a Character already in a Pod: launching, waiting and exiting remain possible; it only blocks new entry (FAQ Rules 3). If an Intruder appears in the Evacuation Section Room while you wait, ALL Characters in its Pods return to that Room. **A second Character who boards your waiting Pod may immediately launch it with you aboard; the first occupant does not reserve control of launch.** Heavy Objects take no Character space in a Pod.
+- **Unlock:** all Pods begin Locked. Unlock manually through Items/Hatch Control, or automatically on the first Character death or Self-Destruct's first yellow space.
+- **Board:** pay 2 Action cards for the corresponding Evacuation Section A/B Room Action. A Pod there must be Unlocked with a free Character space. No entry while the Section contains an Intruder or Malfunction. First roll Noise; an Intruder appearing or reaching the Section makes entry fail.
+- **Capacity:** 2 Characters per Pod. Heavy Objects take no Character space.
+- **Launch immediately:** after boarding you may launch. Remove the Pod token and its occupants' miniatures from the game; they stop participating and count as arriving on Earth. They still face the final Contamination and Objective checks.
+- **Wait after boarding:** you pass the current turn. You remain treated as present in the Section for Noise rolls from bag development (FAQ Rules 1).
+- **At the start of your first round in each later Player Phase**, choose exactly one: remain waiting and pass; launch; or exit for free into the corresponding Section Room and play a full round of 2 Actions (FAQ Rules 2).
+- **A second Character boards your waiting Pod:** that Character may launch it immediately with both of you aboard; the first occupant has no reserved launch control.
+- **An Intruder appears in the Section while you wait:** all Characters in that Section's Pods immediately return to its Room.
+- **A Malfunction appears in the Section while you wait:** you may still wait, launch or exit; the marker blocks only new entry to Pods (FAQ Rules 3).
 
